  "_apa_ini": "Worked-example control. It follows the protocol of the paired track on the same two statistics books, but the two passages of a pair differ in the text itself, a worked example against a definition, instead of in the profile metadata. It checks on this corpus, as FollowIR does on an outside English corpus, that the scoring setup can show instruction following.",
  "status_arm": "post hoc, outside the pre-registered family of eight",
  "label_source": "deterministic (model scores); the textual gold and counterpart are built deterministically from the book structure, with no LLM and no human annotator",
  "populasi": "58 topic pairs, 116 rows, a pool of 71 candidates per row",
  "sumber_buku": [
    "stat-introduction-to-statistics-lane-publicdomain",
    "stat-introductory-statistics-2e-ccby-2023"
  ],
  "instruksi_default_verbatim": "Given a web search query, retrieve relevant passages that answer the query",
  "instruksi_kondisi_verbatim": {
    "contoh": "Retrieve a passage that works through a concrete numerical example with actual numbers and a step-by-step solution",
    "definisi": "Retrieve a passage that states the conceptual definition and explanation, without numerical worked examples"
  },
  "fakta_struktural_default": "In the default arm the two rows of a pair receive the same query and instruction, so their rankings are identical (checked 58 of 58 for all three models) and exactly one row wins. The default pairwise rate is therefore exactly 0.5000 by construction.",
  "uji_primer": "pair-level sign test on the difference in win counts (condition minus default, where default is always 1), Holm within the family of three models, run on the full 58 pairs and on the 36 filtered pairs",
  "uji_sekunder": "row-level exact McNemar; reported in full but secondary, because the two rows of a pair are perfectly negatively correlated in the default arm",
  "aturan_saring_verbatim": "A topic pair is kept only when the title of its source section passes all four conditions below. Every condition is computed from the title text alone, without touching scores, rankings, golds, or counterparts. T1, no PDF extraction artifact: the title holds none of 'GLYPH<', 'font=/', or '<c='. T2, a well-formed head: the title starts with a letter, or with a section number matching ^\\d+\\.\\d+\\s. T3, not book apparatus: the title (lowercased, section number removed, spaces collapsed) is not in the closed stop list S and starts with none of the prefixes in P. T4, topically specific: after the section number is removed, at least two alphabetic tokens of 3 or more letters remain that are not function words F. S, P, and F are listed in full in the daftar_henti, awalan_henti, and kata_fungsi fields of this table.",
  "filter_rule_verbatim_en": "A topic pair is RETAINED only if its source section heading satisfies all four conditions. Every condition is computed from the heading text alone, touching no score, ranking, gold, or counterpart. T1 no PDF extraction artefact: the heading contains none of 'GLYPH<', 'font=/', '<c='. T2 well-formed heading: the heading starts with a letter, or with a section-number pattern ^\\d+\\.\\d+\\s. T3 not book apparatus: the heading (lowercased, section number stripped, whitespace collapsed) is not in the closed stoplist S and does not start with any prefix in P. T4 topical specificity: after stripping the section number, at least two alphabetic tokens of length >= 3 remain that are not function words in F. S, P, and F are listed verbatim in the table.",
  "aturan_saring_ditetapkan": "The four rules were written after the cells were scored. Each reads only the section title, never a score, ranking, or gold.",
